Status - Overview: render the Modem Info card as widgets when the Apex theme is active

luci-theme-apex shows the Modem Info card as a Device widget, a Status widget
(connection chip) and one signal widget per progress-bar entry (RSSI / RSRP /
RSRQ / SINR; LTE and NR) instead of the stock table. A theme cannot supply that
markup hack-free: the card is rendered client-side by this include (owned by
luci-app-qmodem; a second copy in the theme package would be an apk file
conflict) from the modem_ctrl.info ubus method, so the markup has to come from
here.

The theme in use is read on every render from L.env.media (set by the luci-base
header template), so switching themes needs no reboot and no reload logic:
  - Apex (/luci-static/apex): widgets (ax-sys-* / ax-mdm-* classes, styled by
    the theme's cascade.css; semantic dl/dt/dd + h4 + role="meter" with the real
    min/max; all strings via _()).
  - any other theme, or when there is nothing to show / the data is malformed:
    the stock table below, byte-identical to before (verified against the
    minified build; no extra request on that path).
Quality labels (Excellent / Good / Fair / Poor) use generic LTE/NR bands per
metric (RSRP -80/-90/-100, RSRQ -10/-15/-20, SINR 20/13/0, RSSI -65/-75/-85);
the data carries no quality. SIM identity entries are not shown (the stock card
does not show them either).

